    "text": "SECTION 1  \nThe clock ticks slow, a steady rhythm,  \nBut my heart is racing, a frantic beat.  \nThe classroom doors are closed, the lights dim,  \nAnd I’m left in silence, feeling so far.  \n\nSECTION 2  \nI wish I could just step inside,  \nTo hear the lectures, to see the faces.  \nThe professor’s voice, a gentle guide,  \nNow feels like a distant echo in my mind.  \n\nSECTION 3  \nI’ve missed the quizzes, the projects, the tests,  \nThe discussions, the moments we share.  \nEach lesson is a puzzle I can’t solve,  \nAnd I’m left wondering, “What’s next?”  \n\nSECTION 4  \nI long for the laughter, the shared joy,  \nThe knowledge that comes with each class.  \nBut time is slipping through my fingers,  \nAnd I’m left wondering if I’ll ever catch up.  \n\nCan I get my money back for the classes I missed?",
